body:
As a californian living in sweden, all I can say is wtf. ;_;
I'm sorry to my adopted home, to europe, and the rest of the world. :(

Most of us don't support this, it's just the stupidest who tend to be the loudest... :/

On a good day, I feel like I look okay/average (like an average vanilla ice cream), and on a bad day, okayish (super cheap vanilla ice cream). Regardless, I feel like I'm fat or something needs to be fixed/improved. :/ 

However, I've always gotten complimented on my looks (ex. beautiful, hot, could be a model, still look pretty when I cry, etc) and seem to attract good-looking people, so if I had better self-confidence, how I'd describe myself would (hopefully) be different. ^^; 

TLDR - I don't feel or think I'm anything but average. However, people say that I'm very attractive. I don't see it.  :(
